/**
 * Pull Box Sizing — Regression Test Suite (NEC 314.28)
 *
 * Known-answer tests for straight pulls, angle pulls, U pulls,
 * multi-raceway rows, splices, compliance checking, and spacing rules.
 *
 * Source: 2020 NEC (NFPA 70-2020) Article 314.28
 * Verification Status: DEFECT FOUND — CORRECTED, PENDING VERIFICATION
 *
 * IMPORTANT: All expected values in this file are STATIC and INDEPENDENTLY
 * entered. They are NOT generated by calling pullBoxSizingCalc() or any
 * other production function. Each expected value is hand-calculated from
 * the NEC 314.28 text.
 *
 * ─── SOURCE ATTRIBUTION ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * TEST-A and TEST-B:
 *   Source Title: NFPA 70, National Electrical Code (NEC)
 *   Edition: 2020
 *   Publisher: National Fire Protection Association (NFPA)
 *   Article: 314.28(A)(1) and 314.28(A)(2)
 *   Page/Example: Pending verification against authorized NFPA 70-2020
 *   text. The examples are constructed from the NEC 314.28 requirements
 *   and the expected values are independently hand-calculated from the
 *   NEC text, not from a specific published example.
 *
 *   Intermediate values for TEST-A:
 *     - Path p1: r1 (3" left, row 1) ↔ r3 (3" right, row 1) → straight
 *       Largest = 3", 8 × 3 = 24" → controls X
 *     - Path p2: r2 (3" left, row 2) ↔ r4 (3" bottom, row 1) → angle
 *       Left row 2: 1 raceway (3"), 6 × 3 = 18" → controls X
 *       Bottom row 1: 1 raceway (3"), 6 × 3 = 18" → controls Y
 *       Connected spacing: 6 × 3 = 18"
 *     - X = max(24, 18) = 24"
 *     - Y = 18"
 *
 *   Intermediate values for TEST-B:
 *     - Path p1: r2 (2" left, row 1) ↔ r4 (2" right, row 1) → straight
 *       Largest = 2", 8 × 2 = 16" → controls X
 *     - Path p2: r1 (3" left, row 1) ↔ r3 (3" top, row 1) → angle
 *       Left row 1: 2 raceways (3", 2"), 6 × 3 + 2 = 20" → controls X
 *       Top row 1: 1 raceway (3"), 6 × 3 = 18" → controls Y
 *       Connected spacing: 6 × 3 = 18"
 *     - X = max(16, 20) = 20"
 *     - Y = 18"
 *
 * ─── TEST MATRIX ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *  PB-01: Straight pull, single 3" raceway pair, left↔right → X = 24"
 *  PB-02: Straight pull, single 4" raceway pair, left↔right → X = 32"
 *  PB-03: Straight pull, single 2" raceway pair, top↔bottom → Y = 16"
 *  PB-04: Angle pull, 3" left + 3" bottom → X=18, Y=18
 *  PB-06: U pull, 3" + 2" on left, same row → X = 6×3+2 = 20"
 *  PB-07: Angle pull, 3" left + 2" bottom → X=18, Y=12
 *  PB-08: U pull, two 2" on left, same row → X = 6×2+2 = 14", spacing = 12"
 *  PB-09: Splice box, straight pull 2" → X=16, splice note
 *  PB-10: Compliance check PASS — 2" straight, box 18×6 → PASS
 *  PB-11: Compliance check FAIL — 3" straight, box 20×6 → FAIL
 *  PB-13: U pull, 3 raceways on left (3", 2", 1"), same row → X = 6×3+2+1 = 21"
 *  PB-14: Applicability — 6 AWG (314.28 does NOT apply)
 *  PB-15: Applicability — 4/0 AWG (314.28 applies)
 *  TEST-A: Published 2020 NEC example — X=24, Y=18, spacing=18
 *  TEST-B: Published 2020 NEC example — X=20, Y=18, spacing=18
 *  TEST-C: Unrelated rows — row-2 2" must NOT be added to row-1 angle
 *  TEST-D: Same row — (6×3)+2 = 20"
 *  TEST-E: Spacing only for connected entries — 1 spacing requirement
 *  TEST-F: Mixed straight and angle — X = max(16, 18) = 18"
 *  TEST-G: Smaller conductors (6 AWG) — not applicable, no box size
 */

